  "label": {
    "en": [
      "An old monochrome postcard showing a large neo‑Gothic civic building complex on a square. The facades have pointed arches, ornate windows, gables, pinnacles, and a steep roof. People in early 20th‑century clothing walk in the open square in front. Printed captions in French identify the scene as the provincial government building and the post office in Bruges."
